 "revision_b104": {
  "date": "2026-11-12",
  "task": "B-104 (P3 M14; decisions B10)",
  "method": "ITU-R P.526 section 3.2 (diffraction loss for any distance over a smooth sphere): beyond the marginal line-of-sight distance sqrt(2 ae)(sqrt(h1) + sqrt(h2)) the first-term loss of section 3.1.1, F(X) + G(Y1) + G(Y2) with X = 2.188 beta f^(1/3) ae^(-2/3) d, Y = 9.575e-3 beta f^(2/3) ae^(-1/3) h, beta = 1; inside it, A = (1 - h / h_req) A_h where h is the path clearance over the sphere and h_req = 0.552 of the first Fresnel zone, A_h the first-term loss at the modified radius that puts the path at grazing; ae = the Moon's radius (1,737.4 km, no atmosphere)",
  "source_note": "checked against the text of Recommendation ITU-R P.526-16 (11/2025, in force; opened 12 Nov 2026 from itu.int, .cache/external/itu): section 3.1.1.2 equations (13), (14a), (15a), (17a), (17b), (18), (18a), (18b), beta = 1 (horizontal polarization, or vertical above 20 MHz over land), and section 3.2 equations (21) to (25); the G floor 2 + 20 log K (K about 0.0016 for regolith at 2.4 GHz) does not bind; the implementation reproduces the referee's two values (137.0 dB at 5 km for two 2.5 m antennas, 146.6 dB at 3.73 km for two 1.0 m antennas)",
